{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent","id":1012474,"title":"Musings on a Catwoman Exigent","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-05T03:34:57-08:00","id":1012474,"title":"Musings on a Catwoman Exigent","content":"I've had this concept in my head for a while.<br /> Essentially this Exigent has an origin similar to the Batman Returns incarnation of the character where cats swarm around her body and somehow restore her from the brink of death, because say what you will about the movie that scene was pretty memorable. Anyway the idea I'm going with here is that the cats are 'street gods' minor gods subordinate to the City Father or Mother who mostly keep vermin levels in check and make occasional reports so rather than embodying just cat powers there's also themes of smaller urban communities. <br /> <br /> Part of me wants to make it a southern city because Morocco had stray cats everywhere and I kept losing my girlfriend because she'd stopped to pet one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:38:27-08:00","id":1012547,"title":"","content":"If all the minor gods take the form of cats; then perhaps the City Father/Mother is felinoid divinity. Maybe it had a different job prior to becoming the City Father/Mother?<br /> <br /> Also would this Exigent have thief powers feature strongly in her charms as well? Like maybe the minor gods are using a 'black market' Exigent exaltation that was originally created by a god of thieves; but has been mostly reformatted for the minor gods' purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6615-swazzle","name":"Swazzle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T07:36:10-08:00","id":1012572,"title":"","content":"I think the theory behind that scene is that cats are said to have have 9 lives, and if she had 9 lives like a cat then she'd probably recover, and because she's so important to the cats each of them gave up one &quot;life&quot; until she had enough cat lives to make up 9 cat-flavoured human lives. Which does sound quite similar to the idea of exigence in Exalted. Some stray cats actually being minor urban spirits is mythologically fitting too.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of similar scenes in Homestuck, where <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">after John died his body was covered by a swarm of fireflies, and then he woke up on the Battlefield as a god; and after Jade died <i>her</i> body was swarmed by hummingbirds, and then her dreamsprite on the Battlefield ascended into godhood too</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T08:31:29-08:00","id":1012599,"title":"","content":"The cats may have also been the servant spirits or the body of a singular God, maybe God of subterfuge and cats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:06:48-08:00","id":1012676,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you can basically copy-paste Bast into Exalted with few if any changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T03:53:17-08:00","id":1013090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swazzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent?p=1012547#post1012547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also would this Exigent have thief powers feature strongly in her charms as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the reason I like the street gods idea is that it lets me interact with the criminal element indirectly, for these spirits to band together and exalt someone like this implies a common identity that's at odds with the city at large. It'd be surprising if something like that didn\u2019t manifest through crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:59:48-08:00","id":1013238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent?p=1013090#post1013090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the reason I like the street gods idea is that it lets me interact with the criminal element indirectly, for these spirits to band together and exalt someone like this implies a common identity that's at odds with the city at large. It'd be surprising if something like that didn\u2019t manifest through crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, instead of being like Revana Quin, where her powers come from the city itself and further uphold civilization and such, this Exigent might have powers more relating to the outcast social groups, repressed socities, slaves, foreigners, and so on? Which, yes, does heavily imply powers related to the local criminal element, be it street gangs, mafia, or what have you.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the cats have allied themselves with one of said groups, serving as messengers and lookouts in exchange for prayer. Maybe they actively hate the city god and want some change in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T08:27:08-08:00","id":1015680,"title":"","content":"It also seems to reflect attitudes that we saw from Anne Hathaway's Catwoman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:01:44-08:00","id":1015690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent?p=1013238#post1013238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, instead of being like Revana Quin, where her powers come from the city itself and further uphold civilization and such, this Exigent might have powers more relating to the outcast social groups, repressed socities, slaves, foreigners, and so on? Which, yes, does heavily imply powers related to the local criminal element, be it street gangs, mafia, or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though actually I reckon a properly more fleshed out non-QC version of Revana Quin could develop a lot of magical flair with dealing with your underdog and subversive social elements, just 'cos that's what Wu Jian is very much the city of. If her city were Paragon....<br /> <br /> (Also the Cat Spirit Exigent concept is definitely fertile ground, to not be someone who just comes into a thread and chimes in on a lose tangent.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:35:18-08:00","id":1015701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent#post1012474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because say what you will</div> </div> </div> </div>oh I will!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> bout the movie that scene was pretty memorable. </div> </div> </div>It was also a total ripoff of The Crow. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N5uPZ7ocsqA\" target=\"_blank\">Like, not even a thinly veiled one.</a> Just replace every instance of &quot;crow&quot; with &quot;cat&quot;. And the burning crow thing, batman totally stole it. Hacks, the lot of them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway the idea I'm going with here is that the cats are 'street gods' minor gods subordinate to the City Father or Mother who mostly keep vermin levels in check and make occasional reports so rather than embodying just cat powers there's also themes of smaller urban communities.<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to make it a southern city because Morocco had stray cats everywhere and I kept losing my girlfriend because she'd stopped to pet one. </div> </div> </div>What is this matron goddess like? What are her ambitions, relationships, mannerisms, hobbies and passions? What does she fear? What does she feel safe in? What is her wrath like?<br /> Did she have a position before being in charge of vermin? Is her position now a punishment or a promotion?<br /> <br /> Maybe this goddess was once great, like a matron of lions, tigers and panthers and soared to close to the sun, scorning too many of the wrong people with her ambition and getting demoted to rat-duty. she was once bright, shining, powerful and mesmerizing, and signs of that power remain with her through her in the shape of shifting stripes and burning mane-hair -- these attributes can inform Social Interaction Charms, as well as some stealth and awareness (depending on whether the exigent is Ability- Attribute- or Other-based.<br /> <br /> Perhaps she spends most of the day lounging around, like a great cat, soaking in the heat of the sun, becoming active and predatory at night. Perhaps this even affects the way the Exigent's charms manifest (based on time-of-day). This can also come color Resistance, Presence and Performance -related Charms, in that at night safety means the cover of darkness but during the day it means being out in the open among subordinates. Social Interaction can be Charisma-based parties and socializing during the day, and Manipulation-based one-on-one playing-with-your-food shenanigans at night.<br /> <br /> She could be extremely weary of snakes (because cats are hilariously freaked out by snakes), potentially because her biggest rival and hated enemy is a snake-god, who is worshipped extensively in Ixcoatli; this could even introduce a weakness in the Exigent's powerset (if there's an interesting way of doing that).<br /> <br /> <br /> Things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-11-2016, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:02:39-08:00","id":1015710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent?p=1015701#post1015701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was also a total ripoff of The Crow. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N5uPZ7ocsqA\" target=\"_blank\">Like, not even a thinly veiled one.</a> Just replace every instance of &quot;crow&quot; with &quot;cat&quot;. And the burning crow thing, batman totally stole it. Hacks, the lot of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Batman Returns - 1992 and The Crow - 1994 it seems like it would run the opposite way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:13:16-08:00","id":1015716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1012474-musings-on-a-catwoman-exigent?p=1015710#post1015710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Batman Returns - 1992 and The Crow - 1994 it seems like it would run the opposite way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the more recent ones, including Arkham Knight (videogame). Wait, was it also a thing in Returns? I don't remember seeing it and google doesn't reveal anything. If so, I retract that part of the statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"